  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nGeneric method type parameters named like a namespace (#364, closes #348). A generic method whose type parameter had the name of a namespace in its signature or in generated code, such as System, Collections, Generic, Tasks, Imposter, Abstractions or your own namespace, or the name global, got an imposter that failed to compile (CS0234, CS0400, CS0432). The imposter now renames only the type parameter itself in those types, and leaves namespaces and the global:: alias as they are.",
